From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dale Curtis <dalecurtis@chromium.org>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 03:58:54 -0700
Subject: [M150-LTS][Media] Use HeapVector<Member<TextTrackCue>> for active
 cues
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

CueTimeline::currently_active_cues_ previously used a WTF::Vector of
CueInterval objects holding untraced raw TextTrackCue* pointers. When
copied in TextTrackContainer::UpdateDisplay(), the backing store was
allocated on PartitionAlloc rather than the Oilpan heap, meaning Oilpan
could not trace pending cues if synchronous script removed a cue and
triggered garbage collection mid-iteration.

Replace CueTimeline::currently_active_cues_ (and the local cue lists in
TimeMarchesOn) with HeapVector<Member<TextTrackCue>>, trace it in
CueTimeline::Trace(), and return a HeapVector<Member<TextTrackCue>>
snapshot by value from CurrentlyActiveCues().

Fixed: 567936270, 568422505
Change-Id: Ic3d4ee30b0885a7b91dac8d98eb5a37f4471da20
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8503663
Commit-Queue: Fredrik Söderquist <fs@opera.com>
Auto-Submit: Dale Curtis <dalecurtis@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Fredrik Söderquist <fs@opera.com>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1709867}
(cherry picked from commit 082a72b30467b77193ec1cd31614eec5b3df8b3f)

